  message: "REPRO RE-STATED (2026-10-22). WI-lanos's owner decision (option 2) removes the exit-status rows, so the Popen.wait source this repro used will not mint. The recall gap does not depend on it. Re-run on dev 89655df3a3, production CLI, cold cache, claims ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/lanos/claims.yaml, --no-default-overlays:\n  A  child = subprocess.Popen([\"cat\",\"notes.txt\"], stdout=subprocess.PIPE); out, _ = child.communicate(); subprocess.Popen([\"echo\", out])\n       -> exit 3, confirmed_with_caveats, 0 evidence rows\n  B  same, sink subprocess.check_call([\"echo\", out])\n       -> exit 1, violated, 1 row, source communicate\nSo it is still: same value, same source, the flow disappears when the sink callee is the receiver's constructor. Fixtures: /tmp/claude-1002/-home-jgstern-agent-hypergumbo/4068f6c8-e25e-4251-be84-a1fcca3b7abf/scratchpad/hikuz_fx/{A,B} (scratchpad, copy to the notebook before fixing). Which gate drops it is still NOT DIAGNOSED."  # bdf8
